            "highlight_text_color": "",
            "heading_size": "h2"
          }
        },
        "text_BFa6Aa": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Selecting between gaffers tape and duct tape requires a nuanced understanding of their respective strengths and ideal use cases. Here are some strategic insights to guide your decision:</p><p><strong>1. Residue Management:</strong> Gaffers tape’s clean adhesive ensures that surfaces remain undamaged. Duct tape has more of an aggressive adhesive for an extra powerful bond.<br/><strong>2. Temperature Tolerance:</strong> When dealing with high temperatures or heat sources, gaffers tape’s heat resistance gives it an edge over duct tape.<br/><strong>3. Visibility and Finish:</strong> The matte finish of gaffers tape is advantageous in settings where appearance matters. The reflective surface of duct tape offers high visibility.<br/><strong>4. Application Convenience:</strong> Duct tape’s ease of hand-tearing contrasts with gaffers tape’s requirement for cutting tools.<br/><strong>5. Budget Considerations:</strong> Duct tape offers cost savings for budget-conscious projects, while gaffers tape provides specialized performance.</p>",
            "text_size": "text-inherit",
            "text_line_limit": "none",
            "button_style": "btn--underline",
            "button_icon": "none"
          }
        }
      },
